alex: Heads-up — I'm opening a docs PR to expand the Rate limit & 429 troubleshooting surface. Two things I want to capture: 1) long-poll/streaming clients hitting 429s (how to gracefully fallback), 2) concrete SDK snippets for backoff + context-trimming examples. Anyone objections?

maria: +1. please include cURL, node, python examples, and a short migration note for customers using streaming when they move to Dedicated. Keep examples tiny.

sam: I can add node/python backoff snippets. Recommended pattern: use Retry-After header if present (exact seconds), otherwise exp backoff with jitter. Max retries 5. Example:

sam: ```js
// minimal fetch backoff
async function fetchWithBackoff(url, opts){
  for(let i=0;i<5;i++){
    const res = await fetch(url, opts);
    if(res.status!==429) return res;
    const ra = res.headers.get('retry-after');
    const wait = ra ? parseInt(ra,10)*1000 : Math.min(1000*(2**i), 8000) + Math.random()*200;
    await new Promise(r=>setTimeout(r, wait));
  }
  throw new Error('max retries')
}
```

jonah: also recommend logging `x-request-id` and model/route so support can correlate. Add note about not retrying non-idempotent requests blindly.

docs-bot: PR opened: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/892 — alex added initial text + TODO snippets

maria: For streaming fallback: show pattern where client falls back to chunked polling if stream closed with 429. Keep snippet short and explain tradeoffs (latency vs cost + token duplication risk).

sam: I'll add small example showing how to trim oldest messages to fit context window before retrying generation. Pseudocode:

sam: ```py
# trim history to fit context limit
while token_count(history) + prompt_tokens > max_context:
  history.pop(0)
```

alex: Nice. Also add a migration note: when switching to Dedicated, customers may see reduced 429s but still need app-level backoff + circuit-breaker.

maria: Can someone add a short 'when to raise to support' checklist (logs: x-request-id, route, model, timestamps, client-side retries)? I can draft.

sam: I'll push my snippets to the PR in ~30m.

alex: Thanks — assigning this to docs triage. @maria @sam please add reviewers @platform-api

maria: :thumbsup:

jonah: one small nit — prefer `Retry-After` examples to show both seconds and HTTP-date parsing but keep it brief.

sam: good call, I'll add a one-liner note for parsing date header.

alex: awesome. closing thread here, will merge after reviews. Thanks!
